  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Win it back and switch",
  "description": "An area is split into three zones with cones. A team of four stands in each end zone, and one opponent (red) stands in the middle zone.\n\nThe team with the ball makes five passes within the team and then plays the ball to the red player in the middle. Straight after the pass the team steps into the middle zone and must win the ball back as fast as possible – then play it to the team on the other side. Now that team does the same in the other direction. Change the middle player often. Play rounds of about three minutes with mobility work in between.\n\nHarder: one red defender in each end zone tries to intercept the passes and play to the middle player. When red has the ball, all red players try to keep it in the middle zone for as long as possible. For older players: once you have won the ball back, also close the way back into your own zone. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Go to the ball as soon as it is played in – the first seconds matter most."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Press in pairs: one on the ball carrier, one closing the pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Those not pressing shift across so the pass back into your zone is closed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "When you win the ball: look up and play the pass across to the other side at once."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 3,
  "focus": [
    "defence",
    "transition",
    "passing"
  ],
  "phase": "warmup",
  "durationMinutes": 15,
